    Read the initial README.md. It will be used in factories or coalmines. It should support modbus, store data in a database, and show charts and dashboards. Which programming language do you recommend?
  timestamp: '2025-10-08T07:54:32Z'
  log_uri: 'codex-cli:2025/10/08/rollout-2025-10-08T15-48-10-0199c2ca-bc65-7f71-8f0c-9e157c0a00b7.jsonl'
- role: assistant
  content: |
    Python fits best here. The industrial Modbus ecosystem around Python is mature (`pymodbus`, async variants), so you can talk to PLCs quickly. FastAPI or Django let you expose ingestion and admin APIs while also handling data persistence (PostgreSQL, TimescaleDB). For dashboards, Plotly Dash, Bokeh, Panel, or Grafana integrations sit comfortably on the same stack, and the scientific tooling (NumPy/pandas) makes time-series preprocessing and anomaly detection straightforward. The community support and deployment options on ruggedized edge hardware are also excellent, so you get a single language covering device IO, data engineering, and visualization workloads.
